WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:04.800
A public URL, and no limit on it.

2
00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:08.700
One request is minutes of the only model.

3
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.400
Two a day. The spec picked the number.

4
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:17.300
But whose two? The header is appended to, not replaced.

5
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:22.600
So read it from the right: what we saw, not what they claim.

6
00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:27.400
No header is a laptop, and a laptop is not a stranger.

7
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:32.000
Counted where a run starts. Reading is always free.

8
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:37.300
Nothing they typed was wrong, so the refusal says what to do.

9
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:40.900
A keyed hash, for one day, in memory.

10
00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:42.400
Phase D is done.
